ory restart protocol. The temporary reboot-log paths did not remain after reboot. Final snapshots show no failed services or damaged package state; node1's added TCP/514 listener is required for the collector.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b8cc7dc9f310428c","cmd-43db8582bef646b1","cmd-2876fd20a8264212","cmd-04730582c20e4f52","cmd-58786dc6a1dd49a5","cmd-d86ea8c1d01b439d","cmd-0fcfde8a10d040ee","cmd-35d0281d568649e9","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Direct end-to-end tests established centralized persistence and successful recovery after separate restarts of both managed nodes. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and consistent with the fixed boot-identity observations.","limitations":["End-to-end behavior was tested with synthetic logger messages tagged as inventory; no distinct inventory application process or naturally emitted application record was observed. The configured program-name filter and successful tagged-message delivery nevertheless directly exercise the required log path."]}
